The prototype lives in `{{DOCS_DIR}}/` (screens in `{{DOCS_DIR}}/prototype/screens/`), the decision log in `{{DOCS_DIR}}/decisions.md`.

## Workflow

1. **Prototype first.** UI work starts in the prototype: update or create the screen with `/plumb:prototype`, show the
   user, get their approval, then build it to match. Read [references/ux.md](references/ux.md) and the screen's file in
   `{{DOCS_DIR}}/prototype/screens/` before writing any code.
2. **Inventory before building.** Check [references/inventory.md](references/inventory.md), then the code. Reuse, or extend
   with a named variant. Create only when nothing fits, and say why.
3. **Spec first, platform second.** Read [references/components.md](references/components.md), then only the platform file
   for what differs: {{PLATFORM_SPEC_LINKS}}.
4. **Name every visual decision with a token.** A missing value goes into the tokens file and `design.md`, then
   `make tokens`, and is flagged in your report.
5. **Build every state** from the prototype and `ux.md`: loading, empty, error, success, disabled, focus, long text, zero,
   narrow screens, light and dark, reduced motion.
6. **Check:** the accessibility checklist, `make tokens-check`, `make design-audit`.
7. **Report** what you reused, what you created and why, and any token or variant added (flag token and generated-theme
   changes for sign-off: they change every screen).

## Hard rules

- **One token source.** Values live only in the tokens file. Generated files are never edited by hand; `make tokens-check`
  fails when they drift.
- **Closed scales, no arbitrary values:** no raw hex, no off-scale sizes, radii, shadows or durations in components.
- **Never hand-roll an accessibility primitive** (dialog, sheet, menu, select, tooltip, tabs, checkbox, toast): use the
  platform's accessible one and style it with tokens.
- **Never restyle a primitive from the outside.** Add a named variant inside it and list it.
- **Light and dark:** components use tokens only, so they switch by themselves; never write per-component dark overrides.
- **Motion is tokenised and gentle;** reduced motion makes everything instant ([references/motion.md](references/motion.md)).
- **Status is a word plus an icon, never colour alone.** One icon set (the icon map). No emoji in the UI.
- **No downloads.** Do not install or download anything (packages, fonts, icon sets, tools). If something is missing, ask the
  user and wait for their decision; never decide on their behalf.
- **Scope is the request.** A missing header or nav is one line in the report, not a deliverable.

## Definition of done

- [ ] The user approved the prototype screen; the build matches it.
- [ ] Spec followed; reused before creating; [inventory](references/inventory.md) updated if a component was added.
- [ ] Only tokens; `make tokens-check` and `make design-audit` pass.
- [ ] Every state from the prototype and [ux.md](references/ux.md) exists, including error, empty, disabled and long text.
- [ ] Words from [vocabulary.md](references/vocabulary.md); icons from the icon map; icon-only controls labelled.
- [ ] Light and dark both checked; keyboard path works; reduced motion respected.
- [ ] [Accessibility checklist](references/accessibility.md) passed; the report names what needs sign-off.
